{"step_index":85,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T13:29:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-10T16:29:12+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-10T16:29:12+03:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\ndocs/attention-phase-0-1.md:68:  starts transcribing. Each meeting can be paused from the toolbar pill or Live text.\r\ndocs/attention-phase-0-1.md:71:  join the meeting's Live text and the existing Catch up store (which already persists\r\ndocs/attention-phase-0-1.md:108:- Meeting model: start/stop rules, local lines in `transcript`, Live text and Catch up,\r\ndocs/attention-phase-0-1.md:110:- UI: Settings → Transcription tab; teal pill and popover; Live text header with Pause/Resume.\r\ndocs/attention-phase-2-3-plan.md:41:Goal: lines you say appear in Live text and the judge's window as \"You\", for the meeting that\r\ndocs/attention-phase-2-3-plan.md:163:- Decision inspector sheet: reason, evidence lines (focusing them in Live text the way\r\ndocs/native-direct-0.3.0-51-validation.json:7:    \"Transcription pill is its own toolbar item using the system glass as its capsule; announcement text uses the primary colour with orange only for the status, regular bordered Show live text button (dbba75d)\"\r\ndocs/native-direct-0.3.0-53-validation.json:7:    \"Catch-up places undated live text by arrival time; provider times from several keys in s or ms; live text shows times and reactions; catch-up shows line times and reactions (678cb5c)\",\r\ndocs/native-direct-0.3.0-53-validation.json:26:    \"reactions in live text not yet seen in a live meeting\"\r\ndocs/native-direct-0.3.0-84-validation.json:15:    \"Live Text copy acceptance test skips when the OS denies interactive selection in sandboxed environments\"\r\ndocs/native-direct-0.3.0-84-validation.json:34:    \"fullTestSuite\": \"NativeDesktopTests on source f40c4ab: 428 tests, 37 skipped, 0 failures; the Live Text copy acceptance test skipped cleanly because this environment denies VisionKit interactive selection\",\r\ndocs/native-direct-0.3.0-85-validation.json:23:    \"fullTestSuite\": \"NativeDesktopTests on source ac3729c: 451 tests, 37 skipped (Live Text interactive-selection denial), 0 failures\",\r\ndocs/native-mac-recommendation-2026-10-26.md:11:No push notification, notification permission, timed reminder, per-release redisplay, background work, network lookup or native distribution update is introduced. Stable/beta choice stays on the official download page. Native Mac build 26 and iOS share/VP9/Live Text behavior remain unchanged.\r\ndocs/release-0.2.0-build110.md:9:Incoming screen shares support an on-demand full-resolution captured frame with native Live Text selection, Copy, zoom/pan and Back to Live. Meeting controls/audio continue. Snapshot identity survives source changes; timeout/close/leave reject late results and keep expensive work single-flight. Images/text are not persisted or uploaded.\r\ndocs/share-workspace-and-text-2026-10-25.md:11:Select text is available on incoming shared content. It captures one full-resolution, orientation-correct immutable frame on demand, with source/time identity. Native Live Text provides touch/drag selection and Copy. The frozen selection supports zoom/pan, New frame and Back to Live; meeting audio and controls continue. The snapshot remains labeled as captured if a source ends/replaces it. No image/text is persisted, uploaded or copied to the clipboard automatically. Unsupported Live Text hardware receives an on-device selectable transcript.\r\ndocs/share-workspace-and-text-2026-10-25.md:19:A mixed Cyrillic/Latin Live Text check exceeded its deadline under concurrent simulator UI load, but passed in 0.543 seconds in an isolated signed host. The same XPC warning appeared in the passing run; neither a sandbox nor resource-pressure root cause is established. A subsequent full suite exposed a test-only AppKit window lifetime error during teardown; it is tracked in the retained failed result rather than counted as a pass. The native fixture now disables automatic NSWindow release on close. The OCR workflow now bounds UI waiting to 12 seconds, retains its captured image, rejects late results and keeps the process-wide permit until the system operation actually returns. Reopening cannot create overlapping jobs or keep the previous UI alive. No automatic retry occurs.\r\ndocs/share-workspace-and-text-2026-10-25.md:21:Final native suite: 89 cases, 74 passed, 15 explicit skips, zero failures, including the disposable live codec sequence, real bilingual recognition, deadline/lifecycle checks, updater safety and CloudKit/continuation unit contracts. Native compact/wide editor layout and Live Text were visually inspected; bitmap-cache captures omit native control layers, so the live-window screenshot was used to verify real control rendering. Distribution tooling: 18 tests passed. Final simulator OCR/lifecycle suite: 10 passed, no failures. The weak-owner test allows a UIKit layout/autorelease turn and proves deallocation before suspended OCR resumes; production ownership did not require another change. The separately completed affected PresenterCanvas tests also passed. Astra xhigh reviewed the final source and timeout/lifecycle tests with no remaining concrete blocker.\r\ndocs/share-workspace-and-text-2026-10-25.md:25:Per user instruction: no new physical-device run for this release. Verify composed VP9 outgoing camera/share independence, source replacement, thermals/battery relative to Efficient, real touch Live Text selection/Copy/zoom/rotation and source changes, plus call/background recovery while the selection is open. iOS whole-screen ReplayKit VP9 remains unavailable until independently qualified; no battery improvement is claimed.\r\ndocs/telemost-feature-completion.md:33:are post-call account/tariff features. The Live text pane states the limitation;\r\ndocs/ui-ux-review-2026-10-15.md:88:- Chat currently defaults to **All activity**. Reactions history is a filter under Chat within Conversation, beside Live text and Catch up. Text chat can be unavailable while reaction history remains accessible under the Chat segment. [ConversationPanelViewController](/Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/ConversationPanelViewController.swift:84)\r\ndocs/ui-ux-review-2026-10-15.md:100:| P1 | Chat, reaction history, Live text, and Catch up form a two-level filter vocabulary; history can appear under Chat when chat is unavailable (S). | Chat defaults to a merged message/reaction timeline. The bottom shortcut opens the sender directly; optional filters narrow the timeline. Keep receipt diagnostics out of the conversation and retain the composer/reading position. |\r\ndocs/ui-ux-review-2026-10-15.md:306:| Transcript | Live text, Follow latest, available/off/unavailable distinctions | Use clear “Live text” with current availability once; speaker/time structure and one follow control. Do not imply complete transcription or recording. Preserve selection/copy and scroll when new text arrives. |\r\ndocs/validation-2026-09-25.md:33:  Live text, and Catch up.\r\n"}
